# .spun get drop01 through gui-test.py's drop proxy, which closes the
# connection once, at the stage of the run (mame-drop.sh). drop01's install
# directory is suggested, so y at 16 s answers "Install to C:/apps/drop?".
# Every stage ends .spun with an error. ON ERROR keeps BASIC's screen; without
# it the autoexec would end at the error and NextZXOS would show its menu. As
# spun-error.scn.in tells, in MAME the trapped error never reaches line 40:
# BASIC fetches $0000 once a frame with PPC on line 20, the .spun line, and
# the harness logs each fetch as a "reset" line in mame.log. mame-drop.sh
# takes the first of them as the moment .spun ended. BASIC does not print a
# trapped error's message, so the screen shows .spun's own lines only.
put @SPUN@ /dot/SPUN
autostart \x90\x8fGO TO 40
autostart .spun -s @HOST@ -p @PORT@ get drop01
autostart PRINT "SPUNDROPDONE"
autostart FOR i=0 TO 1 STEP 0: NEXT i
seconds 40
key 16 y
snap 9 10 12 14 17 20 25 39
screen 39 Opening @HOST@
